    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10161" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conflictātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		conflicto (postAug.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a striking together, a collision, conflict,
				struggle</i>: exercituum duorum, Gell 15, 18, 3; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">for a place in the theatre,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 3, 8, 29</span></i>
			 Halm: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">improbissimae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 1, 3, 33, § 8</span></i>
			.—In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">membrorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 302, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Of
			verbal strife, <i>a dispute</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hominum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1
					Tim. 6, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A punishing</i>, <i><span class="en">Cypr. Ep.
				7, 5</span></i>.</div>
